problems.problem:
The vertices of a regular $n$-gon with centre $O$ are labelled $+1$ or $-1$. In one move one may change all the signs at the vertices of a regular $k$-gon $(2\leq k\leq n)$ with the same centre $O$ (a $2$-gon is a segment whose midpoint is $O$). Prove that in cases (a), (b), (c) there is a labelling from which one can never obtain all $+1$:

(a) $n=15$;

(b) $n=30$;

(c) any $n>2$.

(d) Let $K(n)$ be the largest number of labellings no one of which can be obtained from another. Prove, for example, that $K(200)=2^{80}$.

There are $1000$ tickets numbered $000,001,\ldots,999$ and $100$ boxes numbered $00,01,\ldots,99$. A ticket may be put in a box if the box number can be obtained from the ticket number by deleting one digit. Prove that:

(a) all the tickets can be put into $50$ boxes;

(b) $40$ boxes are not enough;

(c) fewer than $50$ boxes are not enough.

(d) For $10000$ four-digit tickets, where two digits may be deleted, prove that $34$ boxes suffice.

(e) What is the least number of boxes needed for $k$-digit tickets?

Some numbers are written in a notebook. One may add to the list the arithmetic mean of several of the numbers already in it, provided it is not already in the list. Starting with the two numbers $0$ and $1$, prove that one can obtain

(a) $\frac{1}{5}$;

(b) every rational number between $0$ and $1$.

Points $A_1,A_2,\ldots,A_n$ lie in this order on a line, and each of the segments $A_1A_2,A_2A_3,\ldots,A_{n-1}A_n$ is shorter than $1$. One must mark $k-1$ of the points $A_2,\ldots,A_{n-1}$ so that the segments into which the marked points (together with $A_1$ and $A_n$) divide $A_1A_n$ differ pairwise in length by less than $1$. Prove that this is possible

(a) for $k=3$;

(b) for every $k<n-1$.

Find all sequences of positive integers $(k_n)$ such that

(a) $k_n\leq n\sqrt{n}$ for all $n$;

(b) $k_n-k_m$ is divisible by $m-n$ for all $m>n$.

Do there exist polynomials $P,Q,R$ in the variables $x,y,z$ such that for all $x,y,z$

(a) $P\,(x-y+z)^3+Q\,(y-z-1)^3+R\,(z-2x+1)^3=1$;

(b) $P\,(x-y+z)^3+Q\,(y-z-1)^3+R\,(z-x+1)^3=1$?
